    "explanation": "Rider and driver, this SGD 4.00 no-show charge turns on one fact: did the driver hold position inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius at Blk 79 Toa Payoh Central for a CONTINUOUS 300 seconds, measured from the first qualifying GPS fix at 12:30:00 rather than from the 12:29:55 'arrived' marker? Much of the framework is not in dispute and I accept it. The trip record carries an arrived event, no boarding event, and a driver termination at 12:38:20 coded RIDER_NO_SHOW (not DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE), so POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d) are met; the trace places the driver in the radius around the arrived time, so limb (b) is met; the SGD 4.00 fee is correctly the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (4.00), so there is no fare defect under POL-NS-08(d). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider because the driver replied 18 seconds after her 12:31:02 message, inside the 120-second window. POL-NS-03 is not engaged because the qualifying fixes sit inside the 50 m radius (not between it and the 400 m ceiling) and there is one registered pickup point. POL-NS-05(ii)'s false-arrival referral is not triggered: 35 qualifying in-geofence fixes exist and the 'arrived' marker sits only 5 seconds (half a sampling interval) before the first of them. The rider's presence evidence (36 of 55 qualifying fixes within 100 m, closest 24.6 m) does show she was on site, against the driver's 'nobody came down', but POL-NS-06 makes the rider's presence immaterial to the dwell question, so it does not decide the fee.

The undecided fact is limb (c), the continuous dwell. EV-GPS-00211 (weight 0.39) shows the driver inside the radius continuously from 12:30:00 to 12:33:40 (220 s) and again from 12:36:28 to 12:38:20 (112 s), with a 168-second hole from 12:33:40 to 12:36:28. Both sides' preferred figures fail. The driver's 'longest qualifying run' of 500 s merely spans the hole Ã¢Â€Â” it is a first-fix-to-last-fix span, not a measured continuous dwell Ã¢Â€Â” and crediting the hole, or adding the two runs to 332 s, is available only through POL-NS-06(i), which requires a present, populated traffic advisory covering this road and window. EV-ADVIS-00211-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so neither the span nor the sum is the effective dwell. The rider's figure of 220 s is the longest unbroken run, but it converts the hole into a departure, which the trace does not show either (no fix lies outside the radius; max_excursion_m is null). On the readings the trace actually admits, the continuous dwell is at most 220 s, and whether it reached 300 s is determined by precisely the 168 seconds the trace lost. That stretch is impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(b) Ã¢Â€Â” a sampling gap longer than 120 s inside the waiting window Ã¢Â€Â” and EV-GPS-00211 carries issue codes GPS_GAP and LOW_COVERAGE at weight_multiplier 0.39. The dwell is the deciding fact and rests on this one artifact: the trip record's 8.4-minute wait is measured from the arrived marker (which POL-NS-01(c) says not to use) and comes from the same measurement, and the driver's 12:35:10 chat message, though contemporaneous and sent from inside the hole, records that he was still working the pickup but not where he was, so it cannot carry the in-geofence dwell on its own. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.39, below the 0.70 floor.

I therefore do not rule on the money. The case escalates under POL-NS-09(a) (confidence below the platform floor) and POL-NS-09(e) (the only evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(b)). The SGD 4.00 is held, not collected or refunded, and no driver compensation is paid: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which requires the dwell, which is undecided. The reviewer's single open question is whether the driver remained inside the 50 m pickup radius continuously across 12:33:40 to 12:36:28; if 300 seconds of continuous dwell is established the charge stands and the driver is owed SGD 3.20 (his anti-farming figures clear POL-NS-07: 2 no-show terminations against 146 completed trips, 1.4%), and if it is not, the SGD 4.00 is refunded in full under POL-NS-06. No referral is issued."
